cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Lita: An Auxiliary Language and FLCS Font"
message: "If you use the Lita language specification, or lexicon in your work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software

authors:
  - alias: "CoderTheSheriff"
    email: "karuman2013@gmail.com"
    given-names: "Kartik"
    family-names: "Pawar"

repository-code: "https://github.com/CoderTheSheriff/Lita"

abstract: >-
  Lita is an auxiliary language (auxlang) designed to be comfortable to speak,
  fluid to write, and intuitive to learn. It features a strict Consonant-Vowel (CV)
  phonotactic structure, an ultra-compressed core lexicon of 50 baseline roots
  (plus form particles) expanded through radical compounding, a simplified SVO
  grammar free of morphological inflections, and an original native Fluid
  Logographic Cursive Script (FLCS).

keywords:
  - auxlang
  - constructed-language
  - conlang
  - linguistics
  - logographic-script
  - cursive-script
  - font-software
  - typography
  - oligosynthetic-language

